# P09.23 — Dtor unification: `#[rustc_cxx_drop_wrapper]` +
# auto-Drop for `cxx_class_native!`.
#
# Completes the dtor side of P09.22. Until now, the
# `cxx_class_native!` macro emitted no `impl Drop`: users had to
# wrap the handle in `ManuallyDrop` or expose a manual
# `release()` method, because P09.15's auto-emission of the
# Itanium D0/D1/D2 destructor variants would collide with the
# C++ side's own destructor symbols at link time.
#
# This patch adds `#[rustc_cxx_drop_wrapper]` — the trait-impl
# analogue of `#[rustc_cxx_wrapper]`. Applied to `Drop::drop`
# in an `impl Drop for T` where `T` is `#[repr(cpp)]`, it opts
# that method out of:
#
#   1. The Itanium mangler's `is_cpp_abi` path — so the Rust
#      `drop` body is NOT mangled as `_ZN<class>D1Ev` and can't
#      collide with the C++ side's D1 symbol.
#   2. P09.15's D0/D2 trampoline emission in
#      `rustc_codegen_llvm::mono_item::maybe_add_cxx_dtor_variants`
#      — so the C++ side is the sole definer of D0/D1/D2.
#   3. The NO_MANGLE flag in `rustc_codegen_ssa::codegen_attrs`
#      — so the Rust drop body uses ordinary Rust symbol
#      mangling, not external linkage under a Rust-chosen name.
#
# The `cxx_class_native!` macro now auto-generates
# `impl Drop for T { #[rustc_cxx_drop_wrapper] fn drop(&mut self) { … } }`
# that forwards to an `extern "C++" { fn D1(this: *mut T); }`
# decl. Users of `cxx_class_native!` now get ergonomic automatic
# lifetime management symmetrical with `cxx_class!`.
#
# Files touched:
#   - compiler/rustc_span/src/symbol.rs                       (1 line)
#   - compiler/rustc_feature/src/builtin_attrs.rs             (9 lines)
#   - compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/data_structures.rs         (7 lines)
#   - compiler/rustc_hir/src/attrs/encode_cross_crate.rs      (1 line)
#   - compiler/rustc_passes/src/check_attr.rs                 (1 line)
#   - compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/attributes/codegen_attrs.rs (16 lines)
#   - compiler/rustc_attr_parsing/src/context.rs              (1 line)
#   - compiler/rustc_symbol_mangling/src/itanium.rs           (8 lines)
#   - compiler/rustc_codegen_ssa/src/codegen_attrs.rs         (6 lines)
#   - compiler/rustc_codegen_llvm/src/mono_item.rs            (8 lines)
#   - rustcc/crates/rustcc_macros/src/lib.rs                  (~30 lines; deferred-Drop block → real Drop generation)
#
# Validation:
#   - `cargo test --workspace` → 235/0 (baseline preserved).
#   - `/tmp/p09-23-native-drop/` probe: creates two Widget
#     instances via `cxx_class_native!`, drops them at end of
#     scope, `destroy_count == 2` — confirming each Rust Drop
#     reached the C++ `~Widget()`. Exit 0.
#   - `nm libp09_23_native_drop.a | grep _ZN6Widget` shows D1
#     and C1 as UNDEFINED references, not definitions — the
#     Rust static archive imports them from widget.o.

